Description: Kidux, a Debian for a child's first computer
 Kidux turns a Debian system into a computer a child can be handed: it starts in
 a sign-in screen of its own, gives every child their own account and language,
 lets an adult decide what each of them may use and for how long, and never
 shows a desktop, a terminal or a settings window.
 .
 Installing this package pulls in everything Kidux needs and takes over the way
 the machine starts. Install it on a machine set aside for the purpose, not on
 one someone else is using.
